-- Playbook ve-listing-check: tomorrow's outreach is read first (Sean, 2026-11-01). Safe to run twice.
insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-listing-check', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$BUILD RECORD 3, 2026-11-01 (Logan). TOMORROW'S OUTREACH IS READ FIRST (Sean: "we know we're going to be reaching out to 30 people a day. We can prioritize those people in the check... the day before... So when that potential client clicks on it, they're seeing the information they should be seeing"). Migration 20261101_listing_check_outreach_first.sql: ve_listing_health_due puts first every business in a send day (ve_outreach_batches proposed or approved) for today or tomorrow in Eastern time that has not had its first email, and re-reads it whenever its last check is over two days old. The nightly sweep (2:00 to 3:50 AM Eastern) runs before the sender (9 AM). A business the check holds comes off the email list on its own (trg_ve_outreach_listing_hidden). Website and Instagram only, no Google calls. Proven in a rolled-back transaction: a contact on tomorrow's send day came first; checked a day earlier, not re-read; send day six days out, not read early. ALSO: the Vegans Explore Podcast listing's website (vegansexplore.com/vepodcast/, 404) is now its own Vegans Explore listing (Sean: the official page is the listing), logged in ve_listing_edits; the page shows no Visit Website link for a listing that points at itself, and its Needs support flag is closed.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-listing-check' and body like 'BUILD RECORD 3, 2026-11-01%');
